.page cp 1 copy files and directories

# SYNOPSIS
*cp* [*-rRavfpi*] _SOURCE_ _DEST_
*cp* [*-rRavfpi*] _SOURCE_... _DIRECTORY_

# DESCRIPTION
`cp` copies _SOURCE_ to _DEST_, or several sources into _DIRECTORY_. File permissions are copied with the contents. A symbolic link is copied as a link.

# OPTIONS
@ *-r*, *-R*, *-a*
    Copy directories and everything below them. Without it a directory is skipped with a message.
@ *-v*
    Say what is copied.
@ *-f*, *-p*, *-i*
    Accepted and ignored.

# EXIT STATUS
0, 1 if any copy failed or the operands are wrong, 2 for an unknown option.

# EXAMPLES
    cp notes.txt backup.txt
    cp -r /Hakurei/etc /tmp/etc-copy
    cp a b c /tmp

# SEE ALSO
mv(1), rm(1), dd(1)
